  "id": "boxtidwell-transformation",
  "term": "Box–Tidwell transformation",
  "definition": "The Box–Tidwell transformation is a statistical check used in regression modeling to test whether independent variables have a linear relationship with the model’s log-odds. In plain terms, it helps assess whether a logistic regression assumption about predictor shape is met.",
